WEBVTT

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.570
Look, Ms. Otonashi! The huge
houses, the endless yards...

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:07.070
I'm prepared to buy
it all, just for you!

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.910
How about it? Will this
make your heart content?

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.070
Yes!

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:13.600
But--

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.210
"But" what?

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.050
My...

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.070
"Your" what?

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:19.210
Soichiro is--

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.250
"Soichiro is"?

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:43.550
It's too much!
At this rate, I--

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.360
It's going to
be beautiful today.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.370
Hello? Maison Ikkoku--

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:40.760
Sorry for the last-minute call.
I suddenly found some free time.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.470
Not at all. I'm just
glad to see you.

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:47.500
You haven't changed
a bit since high school.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.070
Haven't I?

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.950
I was pretty depressed
for a while, though.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:57.550
I heard that Mr. Otonashi
had passed away.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.060
I wish we'd had
a baby, though--

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:06.310
You do? That would've
made it harder to remarry.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.320
Who says I
want to remarry?

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:13.820
So you're saying you want to be
single the rest of your life?

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:17.540
You're young, so it
may not matter now--

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:19.270
You got a point--

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.460
Oh, Kyoko, you must have two or
three men waiting in the wings.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.310
I'm not lonely, but...

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.290
I can't quite
settle on a guy.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.910
Can't be helped.
You're Kyoko, after all.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.760
I think you should pin some
guy down as soon as possible.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.130
But I'm not--

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:56.510
Even with the best intentions
you'll forget the past with time.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:00.600
And there's no guarantee that
your man will wait for you.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.010
You sound just like my parents
or a woman at my apartments.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:08.820
They're saying
the same thing?

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.460
They're so insistent that I
remarry, it's driving me nuts.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.080
They have to repeat it,
or you'd never consider it.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:21.100
You might try
listening to them.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:46.530
I'm so sick of it.
Everybody says the same thing.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.460
Remarriage--

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.320
I love you, Kyoko!

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.060
I can wait two
or three years.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:11.980
I'm home.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:14.910
Welcome back.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.320
D-Did you need
me for something?

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:31.390
N-No.
Nothing!

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:44.310
If I chose Godai, it'd take another
four or five years to remarry.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:50.810
Would he wait
that long for me?

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:55.310
I should promise to marry him
and wait for his graduation.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:58.820
But how old will
I be by that time?

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:04.060
They say a girl should have
kids before she's thirty.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:08.000
By that reckoning, Mitaka
would suit me better.

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.720
Am I insane!?
What am I thinking!?

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:18.340
I've got no reason to rush.
They both said that they'd wait.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.320
Godai hardly ever
cleans his room.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.390
Gotta impress
the girlfriend.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:44.500
She's on her way over.

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:48.780
Is she?
And then what?

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:50.840
She's gonna fix dinner.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:57.150
She offered to do laundry, but
Godai said he'd take care of it.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:03.220
Even a loser like Godai can
trick women into doing his work.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:05.760
The nerve of Godai!

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:07.270
Whatcha mean?

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:12.370
To go telling everybody
his private business!

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.470
He never said a thing.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:16.970
T-Then how--?

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.400
The phone's so close to my
door. I happened to hear it.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.290
I see.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:33.060
Then from now on, she can
do ALL of his chores for him!

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.270
That about does it.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.440
That about does it!

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.820
Hello, Maison Ikkoku.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:49.960
Coach Mitaka!

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.140
Today?
Yes?

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.570
Yes, I'm not busy.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:22.290
Godai!

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:25.630
I'm here!

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:26.290
Yeah.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:29.670
I'm so happy! You were
waiting at the gate for me!

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:31.070
Uhh, yeah!

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:37.440
I thought I'd make cream stew.
So I bought some cabbage, and--

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:40.750
Q-Quit that, Soichiro!

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.590
Shh!
Jeez!

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:55.400
They're fine!
Let's do this quietly!

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:56.500
Why?

00:10:58.310 --> 00:10:59.290
It's because--

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:02.210
Look at the happy couple.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.840
Hello.
I'm Kozue Nanao.

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:09.350
Hi there.
Ain't you a cutie!

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:12.190
Mrs. Ichinose.
You don't hafta yell!

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:16.990
What could that be?

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:22.960
Mrs. Ichinose!
Come here.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:23.870
Whaddaya want?

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:27.690
No need to go spreading
rumors to the manager.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:31.530
Why not? You got
something to hide here?

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:34.070
Well, no.
Actually I don't.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:41.410
I guess I can sympathize.

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:42.690
Sure you can.

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:47.750
The manager can be a real
hellion when she's jealous.

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:50.190
Yeah.
Every now and again.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:56.560
So I'm jealous, am I!?
How rude!

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.760
She can do all his cooking
and cleaning for all I care!

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:05.130
What does he have
to hide it for?

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:08.730
So you heard?

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:11.170
You made sure I
heard it, didn't you?

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:14.010
No need for you
to get upset.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.320
Those two're still at the
sweet 'n innocent stage.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.540
I'm not the
Ieast bit upset!

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:23.320
Whatever Godai does, it
has nothing to do with me!

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:28.360
You got your nails done!
What's the occasion?

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:32.070
Coach Mitaka and I
have a date today.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.290
A "date"?

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:34.370
A date.

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:42.070
A date! So you and Coach
Mitaka are rolling right along.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:42.900
What?

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:47.410
Well, this is the first time
I ever heard you call it a date.

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:50.980
You'd say you're just going
out, and it isn't a date.

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:53.240
Now you did
up your nails.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.120
Is that so?

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:04.620
This is the first time I've
ever been in a guy's room.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:07.140
Have a seat. It's not
too clean, but--

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:09.760
Huh?

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:14.440
The wall color's
different in this spot.

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:19.040
I just had that fixed. There was
a hole there for the longest time.

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:21.840
What's that?

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.040
What is it?

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:29.260
Where're you going?

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:31.860
Yotsuya!

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:35.940
What are you doing? Open up!
I know you're in there!

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:39.170
If you bust the wall again,
you'll have to deal with me!

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:40.570
Got it!?

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:46.160
The noise stopped.

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:47.170
Good.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.170
Do you have rats
or something?

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:52.240
Nothing so
cute as a rat.

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:10.130
Thank you for waiting.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:12.990
What? What?

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:17.590
T-This isn't-- I mean--
I-It just happened!

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:20.540
Please do as you
wish within your room.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.440
Y-Yotsuya!

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:30.740
K-Kozue. You're
still h-holding me.

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:34.510
But I was
just SO scared.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.590
B-But you're
still holding me.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:38.560
I'm scared!

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:42.590
Y-You see. T-This
isn't proper--

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:44.970
They're still at it!

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:47.720
Y-Y-Yotsuya!
Stop that!

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:54.190
And that's about
the sum of it.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:59.840
And that sums it up.

00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:06.410
Mr. Yotsuya is so much trouble.
It takes money to fix that wall.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.890
I figured you'd say that.

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:11.590
I am the manager.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:36.740
Oh, the manager!

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:45.540
What's up today?
You're so pretty!

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:50.920
Well, I'll be meeting
Coach Mitaka for a date.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:56.690
You are?
Boy, it sounds like fun!

00:15:57.780 --> 00:16:03.410
I-I see. You are. He won't
be taking you in his car?

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:08.410
Apparently, it's in
the shop for repairs.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:12.920
Besides, it's the man
I'm dating, not his car.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.190
And are you headed
anyplace special?

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:27.370
I was gonna make cream
stew, but I got it all wrong.

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:30.730
So instead, I invited Godai
to eat at my folks' house.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.600
I told her it
wasn't necessary--

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:36.980
My, what fun you'll have.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:50.620
I think this is
the place, but--

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:53.990
But why here?

00:16:55.540 --> 00:17:01.130
It's near the station, right
above a dog grooming place.

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:03.560
"Dog grooming"--?

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:12.210
There it is!

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.750
Keiko? Keiko?

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:18.440
Uh-oh.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:23.670
Oh, dear.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:27.920
Stop that.
Bad girl, Keiko.

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:32.000
Your pants,
they're ruined!

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:34.920
I-It's nothing, really.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.690
It'll only take a second.
Just come inside.

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:39.900
T-Thanks anyway! NO!

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:47.570
My god! It's like Godai
is just USING Kozue!

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:52.520
But a girl can
rely on Coach Mitaka!

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:54.750
I-- Um--
I--

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:58.350
I'm meeting someone
very soon, and--

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:00.600
It'll just take
another minute.

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:10.460
A-Are you--

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:12.290
One second more--

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:16.570
And Coach Mitaka would
never tempt a woman.

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:19.730
He's handsome, so people
mistake him for being a playboy.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.210
But actually he's--

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.420
I--

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:47.420
Yes?

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:50.570
S-Sorry, I'm not very
good with dogs.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:52.980
You can lean on me.

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:56.250
C'mon, Masaki.
Go back to your blanket.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.420
That machine's
paying off way too much!

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.340
The workers here are
too stunned to stop her.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:53.500
Look at that ball go!

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.570
That's a jackpot!

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:56.800
You've never
seen that before!?

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:57.400
Never.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:19:59.030
Look at her
concentration.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:10.690
Thanks again for dinner.

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:12.060
Careful going home, now.

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:12.780
Okay.

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:19.190
See ya later, okay?

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:23.000
Bye, Godai!

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:24.640
Come back anytime!

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:27.730
T-Thanks again! Night!

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:45.480
I got the leftovers.
I AM taking advantage.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:55.480
I shouldn't let this half-dating
go on. I feel bad about it.

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:57.500
I can't.

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:08.020
Manager!

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:15.480
You dropped a can
back there. Here.

00:21:15.820 --> 00:21:17.550
I don't want it.
You eat it.

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:34.780
That looks kinda heavy.
I'll carry it for you.

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:38.070
No thanks. I've no desire
to be dependent on men.

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:40.980
Is that right?

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:43.210
That's right.

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:51.350
Umm.

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:52.980
What is it?

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:55.920
Did you and Mitaka
have a fight, or--?

00:21:57.940 --> 00:21:59.100
What makes
you say that?

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.000
I just got a feeling.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.190
We had a wonderful date.

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:08.030
Kinda strange for a date. You're
coming home with all these cans.

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:10.640
You sure you don't
want me to carry them?

00:22:13.190 --> 00:22:16.310
Is something wrong?
You look a little upset.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:18.350
Are you cold?

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:24.790
What I do...

00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:29.000
is none of
your damned business!

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:33.400
It's a hit!
And it's gonna be a long one!

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:36.900
The center-fielder is going back...
back... to the warning track!

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:40.230
It's out of here! A dinger to
the deepest part of the park!

00:22:44.120 --> 00:22:49.280
I'm sure I'm in the right place.
Why would she stand me up?

00:22:49.920 --> 00:22:51.940
I don't remember doing
anything to make her angry.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:54.940
What's going on?

00:23:20.050 --> 00:23:21.230
Manager?

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:52.910
Soichiro is such a bad dog
going off chasing yakitori!

00:23:53.590 --> 00:23:56.250
Doesn't he know how worried
we all are about him!?

00:23:56.820 --> 00:24:00.570
Next: "Soichiro GONE!?
Yakitori Memories"

00:24:01.590 --> 00:24:03.850
Seeing you turn and look at
me in the fading sunset...

00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:06.320
It brings back heartfelt
memories I had forgotten.
